msgid "Now, the syntax ``AguaClara_`` will link to the specified site: AguaClara_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:260
msgid "References"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:261
msgid "References work by calling any \"target\"- either tags (titles, headings, figures, and tables) or labels (equations). These reference formats work internally- calling something within the same document and externally- calling content in some other document within this same project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:263
msgid "Before you start tagging and labelling content with any degree of willy-nilly-ness, make sure that you are not repeating tags or labels. You can check to see if your tag or label is taken by visiting libraries on GitHub. :download:`Check here for tags and labels: </_static/text_documents/heading_index.txt>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:266
msgid "Document Titles and Headings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:267
msgid "This content should be called with the ``:ref:`tag``` functionality. You can also choose what text will be shown. For example, ``:ref:`This text <heading_links_and_references>``` gives :ref:`This text <heading_links_and_references>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:270
msgid "Figures and Tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:271
msgid "These can be referenced in the exact same way as titles and headings. However, they can *also* be referenced using the ``:numref:`tag``` syntax. When this is done, there cannot be text written that will link to the figure. Instead, what shows up is 'Fig. 3' or 'Table 3'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:273
msgid "Figures: ``:numref:`figure_fluffy_cat``` gives :numref:`figure_fluffy_cat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:274
msgid "Tables: ``:numref:`table_an_example_table``` gives :numref:`table_an_example_table`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:279
msgid "Equations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:281
msgid "Equations are a little different, ``:ref:`label``` does not work. They are instead called with the ``:eq:`label``` syntax. You cannot choose what text displays in the reference like you can with titles, headings, figures, and tables. Whenever you reference an equation, parentheses surrounding the equation's number will be the linked-text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/example_aguaclara_rst.rst:283
msgid "Equations: ``:eq:`quadratic_equation``` only generates a number in parentheses. Thus, this reference is usually preceeded by the word: 'equation.' Like this: Equation :eq:`quadratic_equation`."
msgstr ""

